{"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/commands"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A buffer of changes to a world, recorded now and applied later in the order they were"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recorded."}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryingAWorld"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"While a query or an update visits a world’s entities, the world can’t be changed in other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ways: spawning or despawning an entity, or adding or removing a component, would disturb the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage being visited. Record such changes in a command buffer instead, and apply them with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)"},{"text":" once the visit is over. The following example despawns every entity whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"health has run out:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Health(current: 0))","world.spawn(Health(current: 10))","","var commands = Commands()","for (entity, health) in world.query(Health.self) where health.current <= 0 {","    commands.despawn(entity)","}","world.apply(commands)","","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A command on an entity that is no longer live when it applies does nothing, so two commands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that despawn the same entity are safe."}]},{"text":"Naming Entities That Commands Will Spawn","anchor":"Naming-Entities-That-Commands-Will-Spawn","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" returns a placeholder handle for the entity it will create. Later commands in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same buffer can name that placeholder, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" returns the real handles of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entities it spawned, in the order their commands were recorded:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","var commands = Commands()","let ship = commands.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","let turret = commands.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 0))","commands.addChild(turret, to: ship)","","let spawned = world.apply(commands)","print(world.parent(of: spawned[1]) == spawned[0])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A placeholder stands for its entity only inside the buffer that returned it; the world holds no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity with that handle."}]},{"text":"Commands from Systems","anchor":"Commands-from-Systems","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system running alongside others can’t apply commands itself, because applying them would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change entities the other systems are reading. It queues them with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead, and the schedule applies every queued buffer at the end of each wave of systems."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"Commands","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Commands.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Commands.swift#L55"},"externalID":"s:11WorldModule8CommandsV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/init()"],"title":"Creating a Command Buffer","anchor":"Creating-a-Command-Buffer"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/count","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/isEmpty"],"title":"Inspecting a Command Buffer","anchor":"Inspecting-a-Command-Buffer"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/clone(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(from:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/despawn(_:)"],"title":"Spawning and Despawning Entities","anchor":"Spawning-and-Despawning-Entities"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/insert(_:into:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/remove(_:from:)"],"title":"Adding and Removing Components","anchor":"Adding-and-Removing-Components"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands